        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat(durable): add durable session task runtime foundation",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nThis PR adds the opt-in, local-first durable runtime foundation proposed by PR1. The target failure mode is coordinator silence: long-running session/task/subagent work can continue across many steps, branches, and process restarts, but operators and runtime code need a bounded durable projection of which run, step, child, signal, or recovery state is open.\n\nThis is not a general-purpose workflow engine and does not include Work module, Workboard UI/tools, Task Flow projection adapters, or product-specific logic.\n\n## Dependency Chain\n\nThis is PR2 in the replacement durable runtime stack:\n\n1. PR1: durable session/task runtime RFC v2.\n2. PR2: durable runtime foundation, this PR.\n3. PR3: agent/session/subagent wiring on top of this foundation.\n\nThis PR is designed to be reviewable independently as a core foundation slice.\n\n## Summary\n\nAdds:\n\n- `durable_runtime_*` tables in the shared OpenClaw state DB;\n- SQLite store lifecycle with schema version checks and shared state permission hardening;\n- runtime runs, steps, events, refs, links, timers, and signals;\n- local-first claim/release, heartbeat, recovery, and bounded worker helpers;\n- read-only CLI and Gateway inspection surfaces;\n- generic coordination projection with unsupported write controls disabled;\n- Kysely generated types and guardrails for the new schema;\n- public CLI docs for enablement, env vars, storage, and input retention.\n\n## Explicit Non-Scope\n\n- Work module behavior.\n- Workboard UI/tools.\n- Task Flow projection adapters.\n- Retention/compaction policy.\n- Postgres/multi-worker lease contention.\n- Automatic retry/resume policy.\n- Ledger-only write controls.\n\n## Latest Reviewer Follow-Up\n\nUpdated on 2026-07-02 after rebasing onto upstream `origin/main` commit `133ce01e4a`.\n\nHead: `3e39e28135d81586a2851bc68f5d554527ac70d0`.\n\nAddressed ClawSweeper P1 findings:\n\n- Recovery reconciliation now honors the documented explicit worker opt-in. `startDurableRecoveryWorker` uses the shared `OPENCLAW_DURABLE_WORKER` gate, so `OPENCLAW_DURABLE_RUNTIME=1` alone remains an inspection/recording mode and does not start reconciliation.\n- Future durable schema detection now runs immediately after `durable_schema_migrations` is available and before any `durable_runtime_*` table DDL, ALTER, or backfill work.\n- The branch was rebased onto current upstream main; GitHub now reports the PR as conflict-free.\n\nRegression coverage added:\n\n- `src/durable/recovery.test.ts` advances fake timers with durable runtime enabled and no worker flag, then asserts no shared SQLite state file is created.\n- `src/durable/sqlite-store.test.ts` opens a DB stamped with a newer durable schema version, expects rejection, and verifies no `durable_runtime_*` tables were created before the throw.\n\n## Evidence\n\nPost-rebase validation:\n\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs run --config test/vitest/vitest.unit.config.ts src/durable/recovery.test.ts src/durable/sqlite-store.test.ts src/durable/worker.test.ts src/durable/agent-turn.test.ts src/durable/subagent.test.ts src/durable/fan-in.test.ts`\n  - 6 files, 36 tests passed.\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs run --config test/vitest/vitest.commands.config.ts src/commands/durable.test.ts`\n  - 1 file, 2 tests passed.\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs run --config test/vitest/vitest.gateway.config.ts src/gateway/server-methods/durable.test.ts`\n  - 2 files, 4 tests passed.\n- `node scripts/generate-docs-map.mjs --check`\n  - passed with `docs/docs_map.md is up to date`.\n- `git diff --check origin/main HEAD`\n  - passed.\n\nLive behavior proof remains in `docs/specs/durable-runtime-foundation-pr-proof-2026-07-01.md` and covers:\n\n- disabled CLI inspection returning the disabled message without creating durable state files;\n- enabled CLI inspection creating/opening `<temp>/state/openclaw.sqlite`;\n- disabled Gateway durable inspection rejecting before opening or migrating durable state;\n- enabled Gateway durable inspection reading a real durable projection from the opt-in shared state DB.\n\nFull stack typecheck proof is recorded on PR3, which includes this PR2 foundation plus agent/session wiring.\n\n## Notes\n\nThis PR replaces the foundation portion of #97508 with smaller runtime-oriented naming and a narrower review boundary.\n",
        "branch": "codex/openclaw-durable-runtime-foundation-v2-ready",
